.TH MEDIACONV 1 "2025-01-01" "mediaconv 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mediaconv \- convert images and audio files between formats
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mediaconv
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR
.br
.B mediaconv
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR \fB\-\-output\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mediaconv
converts image and audio files between supported formats. It accepts either
a single file or a directory. When a directory is given, every supported
file inside it is converted in parallel.
.PP
If
.B \-\-output
is omitted, the output path is derived from the input: a file keeps its
name but gets the new format's suffix, and a directory is used as its own
output (files are written next to their sources).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-t " TYPE" ", " \-\-type " TYPE"
Force the media type. One of
.BR image " or " audio .
Case-insensitive. Required when converting a directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-image\-format " FMT"
Target image format (e.g.
.BR png ", " jpeg ", " webp ).
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-format " FMT"
Target audio format (e.g.
.BR mp3 ", " flac ", " ogg ).
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " N"
Encoder quality, 0\-100. Higher is better and larger.
.TP
.BI \-\-bitrate " RATE"
Audio bitrate (e.g.
.BR 192k ", " 256k ).
.TP
.BI \-\-resize " WxH"
Resize images to the given dimensions.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-exif
Strip EXIF metadata from images.
.TP
.BR \-\-delete\-original
Delete each source file after its conversion succeeds. Use with care.
.TP
.BI \-w " N" ", " \-\-workers " N"
Number of parallel workers for directory conversion. Must be at least 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a single image to WebP:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mediaconv photo.png \-\-image\-format webp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Convert every audio file in a directory, using four workers:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mediaconv music/ \-\-type audio \-\-audio\-format mp3 \-\-workers 4
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All conversions succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
One or more conversions failed, or arguments were invalid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mediaconv/config.toml
Optional user configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR convert (1),
.BR magick (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://example.com/mediaconv/issues
